dvE"},"source":["# **Data Transformations [Augmentation]**\n","Data augmentation improves generalization during training; normalization matches ViT’s pretrained ImageNet statistics.\n","\n","Augmentation Types:\n","\n","*   Random crop/resizing\n","*   Horizontal & vertical flips\n","*   Rotation\n","*   Color jitter (brightness, contrast, saturation, hue)\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":40,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419389104,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"kF1v0ZSfOTr6"},"outputs":[],"source":["train_transforms = transforms.Compose([\n","    transforms.ToPILImage(),\n","    transforms.Resize(256),\n","    transforms.RandomResizedCrop(224, scale=(0.8, 1.0)),\n","    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(),\n","    transforms.RandomVerticalFlip(p=0.1),\n","    transforms.RandomRotation(20),\n","    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.25, contrast=0.25, saturation=0.25, hue=0.02),\n","    transforms.ToTensor(),\n","    transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n","])\n","\n","test_transforms = transforms.Compose([\n","    transforms.ToPILImage(),\n","    transforms.Resize(256),\n","    transforms.CenterCrop(224),\n","    transforms.ToTensor(),\n","    transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n","])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"9CqSZOSWOzR3"},"source":["# **Dataset class**\n","This class handles image reading, transformation, and label conversion for PyTorch training."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":41,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":10,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419389104,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"W5J2IbeeOhD9"},"outputs":[],"source":["class BirdDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataframe, root, transforms=None):\n","        self.df = dataframe\n","        self.root = os.path.join(root, \"images\")\n","        self.manual_root = os.path.join(root, \"manually_selected_images\")\n","        self.transforms = transforms\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        row = self.df.iloc[idx]\n","        img_path = os.path.join(self.root, row[\"path\"])\n","\n","        # Try reading from main folder\n","        img = cv2.imread(img_path)\n","        if img is None:\n","            # Try manually added folder\n","            alt_path = os.path.join(self.manual_root, row[\"path\"])\n","            img = cv2.imread(alt_path)\n","\n","            if img is None:\n","                print(f\"⚠️ Warning: Failed to read image at {img_path} or {alt_path}\")\n","                img = np.zeros((224, 224, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\n","            else:\n","                img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        else:\n","            img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","\n","        if self.transforms:\n","            img = self.transforms(img)\n","\n","        label = torch.tensor(row[\"label\"] - 1, dtype=torch.long)\n","        return img, label\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.df)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"E2-KR1-2PZFL"},"source":["# **Split data into train/val/test loaders**\n","Splits data for training, validation, and testing; creates dataloaders for batch processing and GPU acceleration."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":42,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":10,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419389112,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"tDlTBAgVPaLP","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"3457add7-5397-45c0-b41b-5da6e6588c10"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/utils/data/dataloader.py:627: UserWarning: This DataLoader will create 4 worker processes in total. Our suggested max number of worker in current system is 2, which is smaller than what this DataLoader is going to create. Please be aware that excessive worker creation might get DataLoader running slow or even freeze, lower the worker number to avoid potential slowness/freeze if necessary.\n","  warnings.warn(\n"]}],"source":["batch_size = 32\n","\n","train_dataset = BirdDataset(train_df, root, transforms=train_transforms)\n","val_dataset   = BirdDataset(val_df, root, transforms=test_transforms)\n","test_dataset  = BirdDataset(test_df, root, transforms=test_transforms)\n","\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","num_workers = 4 if torch.cuda.is_available() else 0\n","pin_memory = torch.cuda.is_available()\n","\n","train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True, num_workers=num_workers, pin_memory=pin_memory)\n","val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, num_workers=num_workers, pin_memory=pin_memory)\n","test_loader = DataLoader(test_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, num_workers=num_workers, pin_memory=pin_memory)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"6X7d1kW9Pk83"},"source":["# **Model Setup**\n","\n","*   Uses ViT-B/16 model from `timm`.\n","*   Starts by training only the classification head; backbone unfrozen later for fine-tuning.\n","*   Uses mixed precision training for speed and efficiency."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":43,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":1672,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419390784,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"-xJi6tknPdIk","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"8bffcafb-2711-49e8-bbdd-f4593265471b"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipython-input-983281692.py:23: FutureWarning: `torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler(args...)` is deprecated. Please use `torch.amp.GradScaler('cuda', args...)` instead.\n","  scaler = torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler()\n"]}],"source":["num_classes = len(train_df[\"label\"].unique())\n","model = timm.create_model('vit_base_patch16_224', pretrained=True, num_classes=num_classes)\n","model = model.to(device)\n","\n","criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n","\n","fine_tune_full = False\n","unfreeze_at_epoch = 5\n","head_lr = 3e-4\n","full_lr = 1e-5\n","weight_decay = 0.01\n","\n","# freeze backbone initially\n","if not fine_tune_full:\n","    for param in model.parameters():\n","        param.requires_grad = False\n","    if hasattr(model, 'head'):\n","        for p in model.head.parameters():\n","            p.requires_grad = True\n","\n","optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(filter(lambda p: p.requires_grad, model.parameters()), lr=head_lr, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n","scheduler = CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=10, eta_min=1e-6)\n","scaler = torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"k-7ytnZ_P4YH"},"source":["# **Checkpoint helpers**\n","Allows resuming training or loading the best model for evaluation later."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":44,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":6,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419390796,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"Gdq7nLSFPz9e"},"outputs":[],"source":["def save_checkpoint(epoch, model, optimizer, filename=ckpt_path):\n","    torch.save({'epoch': epoch, 'model_state_dict': model.state_dict(), 'optimizer_state_dict': optimizer.state_dict()}, filename)\n","    print(f\"💾 Checkpoint saved at epoch {epoch+1}\")\n","\n","def load_checkpoint(model, optimizer, filename=ckpt_path):\n","    checkpoint = torch.load(filename, map_location=device)\n","    model.load_state_dict(checkpoint['model_state_dict'])\n","    print(f\"🔄 Resumed from epoch {checkpoint['epoch']+1}\")\n","    return checkpoint['epoch'] + 1"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"hwjQQLwcQD2y"},"source":["# **Training loop with validation and early stopping**\n","*   Loops through epochs to train and validate.\n","*   Unfreezes ViT backbone after certain epochs.\n","*   Saves best checkpoint and stops early if validation loss doesn’t improve."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":45,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":1624,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419392417,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"Q9LMCJG6P8_l","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"384e0191-2cd8-41d1-d1cb-712495fca88a"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["🔄 Resumed from epoch 5\n","📈 Loaded previous training history (10 epochs)\n","📈 Loaded previous training & validation accuracy history (10 epochs)\n","✅ Previous best validation loss: 0.4980\n","🎉 Training completed. Best val loss: 0.49797935279574407\n"]}],"source":["train_losses, val_losses = [], []\n","train_accuracies, val_accuracies = [], []\n","start_epoch = 0\n","best_val_loss = np.inf\n","patience, patience_counter = 6, 0\n","epochs = 5\n","\n","if os.path.exists(ckpt_path):\n","    start_epoch = load_checkpoint(model, optimizer, ckpt_path)\n","\n","if os.path.exists(train_loss_path) and os.path.exists(val_loss_path) and os.path.exists(train_acc_path) and os.path.exists(val_acc_path):\n","    train_losses = np.load(train_loss_path).tolist()\n","    val_losses = np.load(val_loss_path).tolist()\n","    print(f\"📈 Loaded previous training history ({len(train_losses)} epochs)\")\n","\n","    train_accuracies = np.load(train_acc_path).tolist()\n","    val_accuracies = np.load(val_acc_path).tolist()\n","    print(f\"📈 Loaded previous training & validation accuracy history ({len(train_losses)} epochs)\")\n","\n","    best_val_loss = min(val_losses)\n","    print(f\"✅ Previous best validation loss: {best_val_loss:.4f}\")\n","else:\n","    train_losses, val_losses = [], []\n","    best_val_loss = np.inf\n","\n","for epoch in range(start_epoch, epochs):\n","    model.train()\n","    running_loss, correct, total = 0.0, 0, 0\n","\n","    if (epoch + 1) == unfreeze_at_epoch and not fine_tune_full:\n","        print(f\"🔓 Unfreezing model at epoch {epoch+1}\")\n","        fine_tune_full = True\n","        for param in model.parameters():\n","            param.requires_grad = True\n","        optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=full_lr, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n","        scheduler = CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=max(1, epochs - epoch), eta_min=1e-6)\n","\n","    pbar = tqdm(train_loader, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{epochs}\")\n","    for imgs, labels in pbar:\n","        imgs, labels = imgs.to(device), labels.to(device)\n","        optimizer.zero_grad()\n","        with torch.cuda.amp.autocast():\n","            outputs = model(imgs)\n","            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n","        scaler.scale(loss).backward()\n","        scaler.unscale_(optimizer)\n","        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), 1.0)\n","        scaler.step(optimizer)\n","        scaler.update()\n","        running_loss += loss.item() * imgs.size(0)\n","\n","        _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n","        correct += (preds == labels).sum().item()\n","        total += labels.size(0)\n","\n","    avg_train_loss = running_loss / len(train_loader.dataset)\n","    train_acc = correct / total\n","    train_losses.append(avg_train_loss)\n","    train_accuracies.append(train_acc)\n","\n","    # Validation\n","    model.eval()\n","    val_running, val_correct, val_total = 0.0, 0, 0\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for imgs, labels in val_loader:\n","            imgs, labels = imgs.to(device), labels.to(device)\n","            with torch.cuda.amp.autocast():\n","                outputs = model(imgs)\n","                loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n","            val_running += loss.item() * imgs.size(0)\n","            _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n","            val_correct += (preds == labels).sum().item()\n","            val_total += labels.size(0)\n","\n","    avg_val_loss = val_running / val_total\n","    val_acc = val_correct / val_total\n","    val_losses.append(avg_val_loss)\n","    val_accuracies.append(val_acc)\n","\n","    print(f\"Epoch [{epoch+1}/{epochs}] Train Loss: {avg_train_loss:.4f} | Val Loss: {avg_val_loss:.4f} | Val Acc: {val_acc*100:.2f}%\")\n","\n","    if avg_val_loss < best_val_loss:\n","        best_val_loss = avg_val_loss\n","        save_checkpoint(  epoch, model, optimizer, ckpt_path)\n","        patience_counter = 0\n","    else:\n","        patience_counter += 1\n","        if patience_counter >= patience:\n","            print(\"⛔ Early stopping triggered.\")\n","            break\n","\n","    scheduler.step()\n","\n","    np.save(train_loss_path, np.array(train_losses))\n","    np.save(val_loss_path, np.array(val_losses))\n","    np.save(train_acc_path, np.array(train_accuracies))\n","    np.save(val_acc_path, np.array(val_accuracies))\n","\n","print(\"🎉 Training completed. Best val loss:\", best_val_loss)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"9ktDnDw9Q8vF"},"source":["# **Evaluation on test set**\n","\n","1.   **Load Best Model:** Reloads the checkpoint that achieved the lowest validation loss.\n","\n","2.   **Switch to Evaluation Mode:** `model.eval()` disables dropout and batch norm updates for stable inference.\n","\n","3.   **Iterate Over Test Loader:**\n","\n","        * Runs model on each batch of test images.\n","        * Uses mixed-precision inference for speed.\n","        * Collects predictions and true labels."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":46,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":19,"status":"ok","timestamp":1762419392438,"user":{"displayName":"Megh Patel","userId":"04599170497738914106"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"bjeqXs70Q9mA","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"1ac43d66-04b5-4a77-ed09-34c21368c489"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["✅ Loaded cached test predictions, labels, and losses from Drive.\n","📊 Average Test Loss: 0.4792\n"]}],"source":